{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex","id":966906,"title":"The limitations of Auspex.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-10T13:49:34-07:00","id":966906,"title":"The limitations of Auspex.","content":"Are the questions you can ask with Auspex the only ones available? It doesn't' say they are, or that they arent. Can I learn Banes? Do you get to passively roll to see if someone is using Obfuscate in your presence, or does it only happen if you suspect and actively start looking? Auspex also adds to your vampire senses, but for some reason it doesn't say this in the Auspex section, so what else am I missing? I hope Onyx Path organizes this stuff better in future books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 09-10-2016, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:54:09-07:00","id":966932,"title":"","content":"Auspex 1 <br /> <i> &quot;This level of Auspex can only answer immediate questions about danger or weakness;the sample questions below cover much of the information the Beast can provide.&quot;</i> PG 128<br /> <br /> Then it provides a sample list of questions. all those questions relate to danger or weakness. So should you ask something like &quot;Are these numbers the winning lotto numbers&quot; it wont work. Or Who is most likely going to get into a fight next week. Wont work either because it is not immediate. It is very much here and now. &quot;Is someone using Obfuscate in here?&quot; would work because that person is likely a danger. Just walking past someone who is obfuscated would not trigger an auspex roll. You have to choose to do all of your disciplines, ( unless I am wrong, excluding the physical buffs, none of them are passive. )<br /> <br /> Auspex 2 <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;This level of Auspex focuses on questions concerning the secrets and weaknesses of a single character.&quot; </i>I would say that if you can find out if they are a diablerist that you would be able to find out if they have fallen to their clan bane. Again the list is an example. Just make sure that what you want to find out is a secret or a weakness. Asking how much someone can bench is probably not going to fly...<br /> <br /> Auspex 3 <br /> You can find out information about objects, you can use the sample list from 1 and 2 as well as the sample list provided in 3. <br /> <br /> As far as what Kindred senses can do and what modifies it... Why would that be in the Auspex section?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:06:15-07:00","id":966941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=966932#post966932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex 1<br /> <i>&quot;This level of Auspex can only answer immediate questions about danger or weakness;the sample questions below cover much of the information the Beast can provide.&quot;</i> PG 128<br /> <br /> Then it provides a sample list of questions. all those questions relate to danger or weakness. So should you ask something like &quot;Are these numbers the winning lotto numbers&quot; it wont work. Or Who is most likely going to get into a fight next week. Wont work either because it is not immediate. It is very much here and now. &quot;Is someone using Obfuscate in here?&quot; would work because that person is likely a danger. Just walking past someone who is obfuscated would not trigger an auspex roll. You have to choose to do all of your disciplines, ( unless I am wrong, excluding the physical buffs, none of them are passive. )<br /> <br /> Auspex 2<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;This level of Auspex focuses on questions concerning the secrets and weaknesses of a single character.&quot; </i>I would say that if you can find out if they are a diablerist that you would be able to find out if they have fallen to their clan bane. Again the list is an example. Just make sure that what you want to find out is a secret or a weakness. Asking how much someone can bench is probably not going to fly...<br /> <br /> Auspex 3<br /> You can find out information about objects, you can use the sample list from 1 and 2 as well as the sample list provided in 3.<br /> <br /> As far as what Kindred senses can do and what modifies it... Why would that be in the Auspex section?</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex dot 3, do you know any useful ways to use this? I have been thinking, but it seems super situational.<br /> <br /> Why would it be in the Auspex section? Because it relates to Auspex. They could have it in both sections it they wanted, but it should be in the Auspex section primarily, because the Auspex section is where you would go to find out what Auspex does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 09-10-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:01:15-07:00","id":966969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=966941#post966941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex dot 3, do you know any useful ways to use this? I have been thinking, but it seems super situational.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Auspex 2 if you don't have witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:19:39-07:00","id":966978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=966969#post966969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's Auspex 2 if you don't have witnesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean you can use Auspex 2 on anyone who has interacted with the object/location just by using Auspex 3 on the location or object? What exactly do you mean there can be no witnesses?<br /> <br /> Do you need to physically be at the location or object, or can you investigate it from a distance through video feed, photographs, records, or description?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:26:52-07:00","id":966982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=966978#post966978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean you can use Auspex 2 on anyone who has interacted with the object/location just by using Auspex 3 on the location or object? What exactly do you mean there can be no witnesses?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I said. I said it's Auspex 2 if you don't have witnesses. If you want to know what happened at some place, you can use Auspex 2. You can use it to find out if John commit diablerie on the Prince, since she was the last one to see the Prince. But if you don't have John, and the Prince is a smear of greasy ash, there is no witness to what happened to the room.<br /> <br /> This is when Auspex 3 comes into play. You can dig the secrets out of the room itself. You can look at the remnants of the broken coffin and use it to find who was hiding inside it. You can pick up a knife and see who it was used to kill and who used it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you need to physically be at the location or object, or can you investigate it from a distance through video feed, photographs, records, or description? </div> </div> </div>I'd say you need to be there without a special Devotion that allows you to do it through pictures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:32:53-07:00","id":966985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=966978#post966978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean you can use Auspex 2 on anyone who has interacted with the object/location just by using Auspex 3 on the location or object? What exactly do you mean there can be no witnesses?<br /> <br /> Do you need to physically be at the location or object, or can you investigate it from a distance through video feed, photographs, records, or description?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people do not think powers work through video. I believe you need to see or touch the object. As far as useful uses.... A body is an object. What killed it? How long ago? Was it supernatural? Is it still here? Was it random ? Did the killer know the victim?<br /> <br /> a murder weapon: Is the owner supernatural? Is the owner the registered owner? so many uses. Like Nofather said. You can use it when you cant ask the person directly. ALLLL disciplines are super situational...<br /> <br /> You're right they could have added a line that says &quot;add your auspex dots to Kindred senses&quot; But we all know they were limited on space. It makes sense that when explaining Kindred senses it would include a list of what modifies it. So as long as you read kindred senses, which every vampire should, you'd know. Not every vampire needs to read Auspex. Not going to argue that point, but that's just my opinion. It is mentioned in Kindred senses and Taste of blood where it should be.. it's listed under a modifier. i<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T01:29:52-07:00","id":967234,"title":"","content":"I find something odd about the description of Auspex 2. In the sample questions, there is one obvious question that you would expect to find and pretty much the main question I was asked as a GM by the player who had auspex : Is the person I'm talking to lying to me ?<br /> <br /> I wasn't sure so I ruled it was a valid question. It didn't come up very often, though because his character died, but yeah, if I played a character with Auspex, that's pretty much the n\u00b01 question I'd be asking, and yet it's not part of the samples. Did they do that because Auspex can't do that or because it was too obvious ? If Auspex can't do that, you'd think they would make a note of it &quot;caution, you auspex can't simply detect lies&quot;. My guess is that it can detect lies or that the person is trying to hide something since it's kind of like some superpowered sherlock scan. I just find it weird nothing is said on the matter in the description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T02:21:44-07:00","id":967241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967234#post967234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find something odd about the description of Auspex 2. In the sample questions, there is one obvious question that you would expect to find and pretty much the main question I was asked as a GM by the player who had auspex : Is the person I'm talking to lying to me ?<br /> <br /> I wasn't sure so I ruled it was a valid question. It didn't come up very often, though because his character died, but yeah, if I played a character with Auspex, that's pretty much the n\u00b01 question I'd be asking, and yet it's not part of the samples. Did they do that because Auspex can't do that or because it was too obvious ? If Auspex can't do that, you'd think they would make a note of it &amp;quot;caution, you auspex can't simply detect lies&amp;quot;. My guess is that it can detect lies or that the person is trying to hide something since it's kind of like some superpowered sherlock scan. I just find it weird nothing is said on the matter in the description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I found this missing odd too. I'd say, yes, it's a valid question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T02:31:24-07:00","id":967243,"title":"","content":"I haven't managed to play many games yet but in my experience Auspex 2 gets used before you talk to someone. That said it counts as a secret therefore I would say yes.<br /> The secrets and weaknesses thing does raise the question would a vampire who didn't know that there was no local taboo on being a diablerist be able to learn that someone was with Auspex if the person would openly tell them if asked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:35:33-07:00","id":967297,"title":"","content":"I assumed that not including &quot;is this person lying?&quot; or some variation was an intentional choice, so that troupes could use their own best judgment and decide for themselves if it's a valid question. In 1e (at least in the MET version) there was a sidebar discussing the implications of allowing Auspex 2 to detect lies or not, and instructing groups to do what works for them. Simply not including it in the sample questions seems to accomplish the same end in significantly less wordcount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:50:39-07:00","id":967307,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, but 1e Auspex 2 was more simple in the way that it gave you pretty much always the same kind of information. You could easily ask a question or pressure someone and then check their aura. It wouldn't say exactly if they lied or not, but you could deduce some easy stuff from there.<br /> <br /> I don't see why auspex 2 would have to be used before you talk to someone. To me, you use it whenever you feel like it. Talking to someone and then checking how your words affected them seems legit and intelligent. Plus, it seems way more useful than knowing what their requiem/dirge is.<br /> <br /> Well, anyway, considering you can force people to tell their whole life stories with clever uses of dominate and majesty, it seems fair you should be able to use Auspex to know if they're fucking with you or not. The real tricky part is : Once you yourself know they're lying, can you use that knowledge in a meaningful way ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:28:18-07:00","id":967329,"title":"","content":"I have a field day with those kinds of players. I never allow that question to stand on its own because the answer to that question is always yes and it's too broad. And unless you phrase the question in a manner of searching for a specific weakness the answer is worthless. Every statement coming out of their mouth could be the gospel truth but the name you know him by is a lie. Or he lied by omitting a detail or exaggerating or because you've been a douchebag to him in the past and it amuses him to send you on a wild goose chase. Maybe he successfully charmed you and since we're talking about two unresistable vampire powers at work and that one lets you get away with lying with impunity. Or he has Obfuscate active so you don't know if he lied to you specifically about what you demanded or he's just lying in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:37:51-07:00","id":967335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967307#post967307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah, but 1e Auspex 2 was more simple in the way that it gave you pretty much always the same kind of information. You could easily ask a question or pressure someone and then check their aura. It wouldn't say exactly if they lied or not, but you could deduce some easy stuff from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't comparing to how it worked in 1e, I was comparing to the sidebar specifically. Putting in a sidebar about &quot;can this power be used to detect lies&quot;, examining the implications of either interpretation, and recommending that groups work out amongst themselves whether it can or can't is one way to leave it open to ST discretion. Not including &quot;is this character lying?&quot; in the sample questions but clearly stating that the list is not exhaustive is another way of leaving it up to ST discretion. The latter does require a lot fewer words, which I assume is why they handled it that way in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:06:30-07:00","id":967351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=966941#post966941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex dot 3, do you know any useful ways to use this? I have been thinking, but it seems super situational.</div> </div> </div> </div> Auspex 3 is basically post-cognition. Doesn't have to be in the form of a vision, but you do get some useful information. What did that vampire do yesterday? Touch something she wore. What is the code for this keypad, or computer password? Touch and find out. Has my Touchstone met any other vampires? How did he feel about the experience? Touch him and find out. Is this the murder weapon? How did the killing happen? <br /> <br /> You get the idea. If its somehow related to the past, you can use Spirit's Touch in some way to get answers. Its an insanely powerful tool for investigation; it can also double as a social bonus if your ST is using the CofD core book and uses the Auspex roll as a Clue that you can use as a dice bonus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:20:42-07:00","id":967390,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Auspex 3 is completely OP for investigations. I guess a really powerful vampire who likes to sit back and boss people around might not get to use it that much, but anybody that has to do any amount of legwork will find it invaluable (well, unless the GM feels like being a bit of a dick and doesn't give out anything).<br /> <br /> The biggest limits it has now is because Obfuscate has had its uses broadened a bit. I also think it's a good opportunity to develop a few devotions for paranoid people. Like how about a Dominate 3 Auspex 3 devotion that imprints a dominate order on an object as a trap for the next Auspex-happy neonate who wants to be clever and spirit touch the big murder weapon in the middle of the room ? They pick it up, start concentrating and all they see is the ventrue's eyes digging into theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:21:50-07:00","id":967391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967234#post967234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find something odd about the description of Auspex 2. In the sample questions, there is one obvious question that you would expect to find and pretty much the main question I was asked as a GM by the player who had auspex : Is the person I'm talking to lying to me ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first use of the ability per scene is free, every other use costs a Vitae.<br /> <br /> That seems like a waste of a power when you can simply use your mundane Skills to figure out whether someone's being true or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-11-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:42:27-07:00","id":967401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967329#post967329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a field day with those kinds of players. I never allow that question to stand on its own because the answer to that question is always yes and it's too broad. And unless you phrase the question in a manner of searching for a specific weakness the answer is worthless. Every statement coming out of their mouth could be the gospel truth but the name you know him by is a lie. Or he lied by omitting a detail or exaggerating or because you've been a douchebag to him in the past and it amuses him to send you on a wild goose chase. Maybe he successfully charmed you and since we're talking about two unresistable vampire powers at work and that one lets you get away with lying with impunity. Or he has Obfuscate active so you don't know if he lied to you specifically about what you demanded or he's just lying in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless I am very wrong, Obfuscate doesnt allow you to lie better... However you can use Auspex to break Obfuscate with a class of wills. If he has you charmed and you use Auspex to figure out if he is fucking you over, then it would be a clash of wills. But if your charmed, to even want to use auspex to find out would take an extremely paranoid person. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12094_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12094\" data-vbnamecard=\"12094\">K9ine</a> ^ neither of those things are listed in Auspex but are mentioned in Obfuscate and implied in Clash of wills ( respectively)<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7104\" data-vbnamecard=\"7104\">S. Brechen</a> Knowing if someone is lying and knowing their dirge are equally useful, but not in every situation. If you plan to manipulate someone over the long run, knowing that they are, say, a junkie is exponentially more useful than if they lied to you just now. As mentioned before, Disciplines and their uses are super situational. You need to be creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:07:13-07:00","id":967412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967401#post967401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I am very wrong, Obfuscate doesnt allow you to lie better...</div> </div> </div> </div> Majesty, however, does. As does a Carthian Law, I think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:12:00-07:00","id":967454,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate 1 conceals your Predatory Aura. You're trying to pass yourself off as a non kindred to other kindred, hence you're lying. And yes, you can attempt a clash of wills but ties go to the defender. I don't allow knowing beforehand someone is kindred to count as an automatic victory or &quot;immunity&quot; to its application. And the reason you've outlined with Majesty is pretty much why I don't assume Auspex is remotely an infallible lie detector. You're auto charmed within seconds after walking in the room. Unless you have prior experience with that individual being a liar or your character is cynical in nature and you successfully lashed out BEFORE they charmed you, you're still stuck believing whatever line they decided to feed you. Rinse and repeat with things like Mesmerize, where you can't even remember what they said or even if they lied or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:43:14-07:00","id":967469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967412#post967412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Majesty, however, does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it makes the subject(s) more inclined to trust you. Which I guess has the same effective result, though it goes about it by making others more inclined to believe your lies rather than by making them more believable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967412#post967412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As does a Carthian Law, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you are referring to Plausible Deniability? Yeah, Carthian Law is weird. My understanding is that Carthians have some special pull with the metaphysical concept of law. And they can leverage that in various ways, including twisting the letter of the law up in knots to preserve the appearance of their own innocence on technicalities and legalese.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:32:00-07:00","id":967564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967469#post967469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you are referring to Plausible Deniability? Yeah, Carthian Law is weird. My understanding is that Carthians have some special pull with the metaphysical concept of law. And they can leverage that in various ways, including twisting the letter of the law up in knots to preserve the appearance of their own innocence on technicalities and legalese.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was more about democracy and the mob than the law itself. If everything's based off the concept of predatory auras, it's combining your auras together and putting them to a single focus about certain things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:37:13-07:00","id":967567,"title":"","content":"Ninja'ed. Was about to nitpick that point as well, though I was going to say it was Justice they influenced. Law is just the most commonly presumed aspect of Justice. I like your point about aura collection better though; it is less 'Mage is right' and more 'Vampires taint stuff'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T04:24:13-07:00","id":967858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967469#post967469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it makes the subject(s) more inclined to trust you. Which I guess has the same effective result, though it goes about it by making others more inclined to believe your lies rather than by making them more believable.</div> </div> </div> </div> Same thing, really. Vampire powers work on the principle of coercion, on forcing people to do what you want. So, you make yourself a better liar not by buffing your dice pool (which Majesty does anyways by forcing people to admire you) but by compelling people to believe you. Most powers represent using force on others in some way, so naturally the &quot;be better liar&quot; power should involve messing with people to do what you want in some way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I assume you are referring to Plausible Deniability? </div> </div> </div>I think there's more coming up in Secrets of the Covenants as well, but yeah. Odd things with lies and half truths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T07:20:32-07:00","id":967914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967469#post967469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it makes the subject(s) more inclined to trust you. Which I guess has the same effective result, though it goes about it by making others more inclined to believe your lies rather than by making them more believable.<br /> <br /> <br /> I assume you are referring to Plausible Deniability? Yeah, Carthian Law is weird. My understanding is that Carthians have some special pull with the metaphysical concept of law. And they can leverage that in various ways, including twisting the letter of the law up in knots to preserve the appearance of their own innocence on technicalities and legalese.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Charmed condition allows you to add your Majesty rating to Manipulation rolls to Subterfuge (and a few other skills, persuasion isn't listed for it as one though) AND your target gets a penalty equal to the users Majesty rating to sense motive or detect their true agenda. So Majesty makes its users a better liar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:48:10-07:00","id":967992,"title":"","content":"No one is debating if Majesty makes you a better liar, it does. Awe gives you bonuses and Charmed makes it feel like whatever they say is truth, but the Original poster said OBFUSCATE makes you a better liar. I think we just got lost. <br /> <br /> Hiding your predatory aura doesnt make you a &quot;liar&quot;. Hiding my natural hair color by dying it doesnt make me a liar. Putting long sleeves over scars and tattoos doesnt make you a liar either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T04:32:23-07:00","id":968451,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone is disagreeing that Obfuscate can block Auspex 2. In fact, if you can target someone or something with Auxpex 2/3, shouldn't you already have broken past the Obfuscate in the first place?* Rather, considering the entire purpose of the thread, a new question arose - should should Auspex and Majesty cause a clash of wills over lying? <br /> <br /> * That's assuming we're talking about using the first, second, or third dot powers. Familar Stranger works differently by placing an illusion over an object or person - how would you cause a Clash of Wills via Auspex with that? That's a form of deception beyond the standard &quot;don't notice me&quot; ability, so it requires a completely different method of interaction with Auspex. Is presenting yourself as someone else a lie by omission in this case? Can that be picked up by Aura Sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:57:20-07:00","id":968519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=967329#post967329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a field day with those kinds of players. I never allow that question to stand on its own because the answer to that question is always yes and it's too broad. And unless you phrase the question in a manner of searching for a specific weakness the answer is worthless. Every statement coming out of their mouth could be the gospel truth but the name you know him by is a lie. Or he lied by omitting a detail or exaggerating or because you've been a douchebag to him in the past and it amuses him to send you on a wild goose chase. Maybe he successfully charmed you and since we're talking about two unresistable vampire powers at work and that one lets you get away with lying with impunity. Or he has Obfuscate active so you don't know if he lied to you specifically about what you demanded or he's just lying in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would personally clarify the intention with the player; it's not really conducive to good game-play in my experience to act like an evil genie trying to twist my player's wishes dependent on their wording. That's something for NPCs to do to the PCs.<br /> <br /> e.g.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are they lying?&quot;<br /> &quot;How do you mean? Are they lying at this moment or have they ever lied to you?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:45:50-07:00","id":968616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/966906-the-limitations-of-auspex?p=968519#post968519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would personally clarify the intention with the player; it's not really conducive to good game-play in my experience to act like an evil genie trying to twist my player's wishes dependent on their wording. That's something for NPCs to do to the PCs.<br /> <br /> e.g.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Are they lying?&amp;quot;<br /> &amp;quot;How do you mean? Are they lying at this moment or have they ever lied to you?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just tell them &quot;you probably won't get any useful information with that question, vampires are pretty much always lying about something - if he's even using an alias that would come up a yes.&quot; Like, that's a perfectly fine way to rule that Auspex works if you want to run it that way, but inform the players so they don't feel cheated when they finally realize that's what's going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}